cription clarifying.\n\nActually, let me reconsider: maybe merge into matrix_tables exactly as-is with columns: meter_size, accuracy_class, q1_minimum, q2_transitional, q3_permanent, q4_overload, q3_q1_ratio. Two tables named by power config.\n\n2. model_family.models: one per size (15), with attributes: {\"accuracy_classes\": [...], \"power_supply\": [...]}. Hmm, accuracy classes per size: DN40 [1,2], DN50 [1,2], DN65 [1,2], DN80 [1,2], DN100 [1,2], DN125 [1,2], DN150 [1,2], DN200 [1,2], DN250 [1,2], DN300 [1,2], DN350 [1,2], DN400 [1,2], DN450 [1,2], DN500 [1,2], DN600 [1,2]. All sizes have both classes (via \"1 & 2\" or separate rows). Power: all sizes available in both AC mains and battery/renewable? Check AC table sizes: 40,50,65,80,100,125,150,200,250,300,350,400,450,500,600 — all 15. Battery table: 40,50,65,80,100,125,150,200,250,300,350,400,450,500,600 — all 15. Yes.\n\n3. characteristics.model_level: \n   - permanent_flow_rate_q3: values per model (size), unit m³/h: DN40:25, DN50:40, DN65:63, DN80:100, DN100:160, DN125:160, DN150:400, DN200:630, DN250:1000, DN300:1600, DN350:1600, DN400:2500, DN450:2500, DN500:4000, DN600:6300.\n   - overload_flow_rate_q4: 31.25, 50, 78.75, 125, 200, 200, 500, 787.5, 1250, 2000, 2000, 3125, 3125, 5000, 7875.\n\n4. characteristics.config_level for Q1/Q2/ratio varying by class and power? This would be large. Alternatively include them only in matrix_tables. I think putting Q1/Q2/ratio only in matrix_tables is acceptable given matrix_tables purpose. But the R137 example populated model_level from the matrix. Hmm.\n\nGiven \"MOST IMPORTANT\" rule 4 emphasizes extracting matrices into model_level, I should make an effort. The problem: 3 dims (size, class, power). Approach: model_id = size (models), config axis 1 = accuracy class, config axis 2 = power supply. For q1: config_level entry with axis \"accuracy_class × power_supply\" and conditions \"class 1, AC mains, DN40\"... no.\n\nAlternative: make models = size+class combos (\"